A tall clear plastic 16oz iced coffee cup, centred and upright, floating against a completely flat matte lilac background of solid colour #D0B9D3 with uniform unshaded colour across the entire frame, no surface, no horizon, no shadow beneath the cup.

The cup is filled with a layered oat milk latte: deep coffee brown at the base graduating to warm golden caramel, topped with a pale cream foam cap and a fine dusting of cinnamon on the surface.

Printed on the front face of the cup, exactly as in the reference image and completely unaltered: a hand-drawn lilac cow with a black tail and black ear patch, below it the chunky rounded bubble-lettering wordmark HUGO in black, and below that a small line of black text reading "The Usual — House Oat Latte". This printed artwork is preserved pixel for pixel from the reference: identical letterforms, identical spelling, identical spacing, identical weight and position. The lettering is hand-drawn artwork and must never be redrawn, re-typeset, straightened, cleaned up or replaced with a font.

Framing: the cup occupies only the central 40 percent of the image width and sits low in the frame with its base near the bottom edge. The entire top 40 percent of the image is empty flat lilac. Generous empty lilac margin on the left and right.

Lighting: warm directional light from the upper right, a soft specular highlight running down the left edge of the clear plastic, even consistent exposure.

Camera: locked-off tripod, straight-on eye-level product shot, 85mm lens, f/5.6, static framing.

The liquid is perfectly still and level. No ice cubes. No splash. No droplets. No motion.

No hand, no fingers, no people, no countertop, no props, no background objects, no additional text, no watermark, no gradient, no vignette, no drop shadow, no reflection, no lens flare.
